body:
Found by V33s suite, reproduced directly by me: gpu/hwcodec/shim/n2shim_format.c:670 (`body[np + i] = 0;` in emit_int) writes past `char body[PREC_MAX + 80]` (480 bytes) when the format has the 0 flag, no precision, and a width larger than the body.

Repro (standalone, links only n2shim_format.c):
  guest fmt "%0500d", one int arg 1
  n2fmt(&c, out, sizeof out, fmt_guest, &a)
  -> UBSan: shim/n2shim_format.c:670:3: runtime error: index 480 out of bounds for type char[480]
Same with any width above ~470 (`%0479d` is already at the edge; `%999999999d` is a full stack smash attempt). The precision is capped at 400 and the format at 2047, but the width is not capped, and this loop adds `width - total` zeros to `zeros` and then writes them into `body`.

Impact: a guest format string (the vendor code and any client of V33/V34 printf) can overflow a 480-byte stack buffer in the shim. The output path is truncated/streamed by emit_field, so the fix is easy:

  if (s->zero && !s->left && s->prec < 0) {
      int total = np + zeros + nd;
      int width = s->width < 0 ? 0 : s->width;
      if (total < width) {
          int extra = width - total;
          int room = (int)sizeof(body) - np - nd;
          if (extra > room) extra = room;   /* emit_field pads the rest, O(1) */
          zeros += extra;
      }
  }

(emit_field already handles `s->zero && allow_zero` with opad, so capping the pre-added zeros preserves the output byte for byte; a test with %0500d and %0999999999d should be added. The alternative is to drop the pre-add entirely and let emit_field do all zero padding.)

This is a real defect in a package I had accepted, so V30s verdict becomes accept with findings (F15) in review/r1/FINDINGS.md until this is fixed. V33s run_tests.sh currently fails only because of this line (N2TEST V33 FAIL asan); the V33 code itself is not implicated.
